ia": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-29T18:12:17Z", "username": "Abhishek Vats", "text": "5. Mariner 10 was the first spacecraft to ever use Gravity Assist (the \"slingshot\" maneuver to reach another planet. Scientists realized they didn't have a rocket powerful enough to send a probe directly to X. Instead, they aimed for a step closer to Y. By flying past Y, the planet's gravity pulled on the craft, slowing it down and \"dropping\" its orbit closer to ____ so it could intercept X. This maneuver is now the gold standard for reaching the outer planets (like Voyager and Cassini), but Mariner 10 was the brave \"guinea pig.” Before Mariner 10, scientists assumed X was a \"dead\" rock like the Moon, with no magnetic field. As the probe flew past, its magnetometer spiked. X actually had a magnetic field, implying it has a partially liquid iron core. Id X. ‎", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-29T18:12:26Z", "username": "Abhishek Vats", "text": "Need only X", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-29T18:12:37Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "mercury", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-29T18:12:45Z", "username": "Abhishek Vats", "text": "Mercury is correct", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-29T18:12:55Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "y is venus", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-29T18:12:55Z", "username": "Abhishek Vats", "text": "Pavan 40 Nikhil 10", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}]